    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1005">

                <pb facs="0673" n="601" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg601"/>

                <head>Inhabitants of Thun</head>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thun</hi></placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_imprecise-inferred-from-sibling-dates" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1865-05-15T23:59:59+00:34" notBefore="1865-05-14T00:00:00+00:34"
                        when="1865-05"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi>, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>The undersigned authorities, societies and private individuals in the district of
                    Thun, rejoicing over the final victory of human rights and the end of the civil
                    war in the American Union, on the one part, and lamenting the murder of the
                    greatest man in the nation, on the other hand, feel it their duty to join
                    cordially in the address to the American people and their leader in the cause of
                    freedom and humanity in our sister republic beyond the ocean.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>HEINRICH HOFER, <hi rendition="#italic">President</hi>.</item>
                            <item>A. KREBSER, <hi rendition="#italic">Notary</hi>.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>(280 other signatures.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
